{number: 155}
{title: I’ll Fly Away}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Some glad morning when this life is o’er,
[F] I’ll fly a-[C] way;
To a home on God’s celestial shore,
[G7] I’ll fly a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] I’ll fly away, O glory,
[F] I’ll fly a-[C] way;
When I die, hallelujah, by and by,
[G7] I’ll fly a-[C] way.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] the shadows of this life have gone,
[F] I’ll fly a-[C] way;
Like a bird from prison bars has flown,
[G7] I’ll fly a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Just [C] a few more weary days and then,
[F] I’ll fly a-[C] way;
To a land where joys shall never end,
[G7] I’ll fly a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}
